# Knowledge base maintenance

## Source of truth

[`docs/KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md`](docs/KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md) is the project knowledge base for humans and agents.

## When you commit

Before creating a git commit that changes behavior, architecture, APIs, auth/roles, deploy, or shared UX patterns:

1. Update the relevant sections in `docs/KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md` (not only the Recent commits list).
2. Stage `docs/KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md` with the same commit.
3. Optionally run `./scripts/kb-append-commit.sh` after commit to append the mechanical log line (or let `.githooks/post-commit` do it).

## Skip KB content edits only when

- Typo-only / comment-only / pure formatting
- Lockfile-only or generated artifact churn

Still prefer a Recent commits line for non-trivial fixes.

## Do not put in the KB

- Secrets, API keys, production DB passwords
- Long code dumps (link to paths instead)
